A recommendation is a category-B-recommendation and is an evidence-type-3-recommendation.
If a patient has an acute-pain and a nonopioid-therapy is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonopioid-therapy for the acute-pain.
If an opioid-benefit does not likely outweigh an opioid-risk then every clinician should not consider an opioid-therapy for an acute-pain.
Every clinician should discuss a realistic-benefit with a patient before an opioid-prescription and should discuss a known-risk with a patient before an opioid-prescription.
